1
00:00:02,026 --> 00:00:10,138
There's a place in Asia where your macaroni doesn't come with cheese, but in soup.

2
00:00:10,138 --> 00:00:15,874
China and its cuisine are incredibly diverse.

3
00:00:15,874 --> 00:00:32,326
We travel from city to city, to uncover the local food scene and meet the people behind it.

4
00:00:32,326 --> 00:00:43,158
This time, we'll go to Hong Kong.

5
00:00:43,158 --> 00:00:47,398
If you don't know what to eat, just pop into a cha chaan teng.

6
00:00:47,398 --> 00:00:52,939
These casual, squeezy cafes offer Hong Kong-style fast food meals for less than $10.

7
00:00:52,939 --> 00:00:57,384
【粤语】My favorites are satay beef noodles and milk tea.

8
00:00:57,384 --> 00:01:04,767
【粤语】I usually order milk tea when I go to a cha chaan teng.

9
00:01:04,767 --> 00:01:09,375
【粤语】Every cha chaan teng has a distinctive taste.

10
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:14,219
【粤语】Some milk teas are sweeter, some have a stronger tea flavor.

11
00:01:14,219 --> 00:01:20,878
【粤语】That's what makes the culture unique to Hong Kong.

12
00:01:20,878 --> 00:01:25,474
[English] Milk tea is essential.

13
00:01:25,474 --> 00:01:40,184
Locals learned to make it when they were under British rule.

14
00:01:40,184 --> 00:01:43,458
We are at the city's oldest existing Cha chaan teng.

15
00:01:43,458 --> 00:01:48,063
It's said that Hong Kong-style milk tea was invented here.

16
00:01:48,063 --> 00:01:49,202
[粤语] My name is Lam Chun-yip.

17
00:01:49,202 --> 00:01:53,803
My brother and I are the second-generation owners of Lan Fong Yuen.

18
00:01:53,803 --> 00:01:59,905
Our silky milk tea is famous in mainland China and Southeast Asia.

19
00:01:59,905 --> 00:02:02,788
Basically any place with a Chinese community knows us.

20
00:02:02,788 --> 00:02:07,753
My dad started the business when he first came to Hong Kong in the early 1940s.

21
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:10,524
Milk tea wasn't popular in Hong Kong yet.

22
00:02:10,524 --> 00:02:15,103
Ships would dock at the Hong Kong pier, and sailors would give my dad tea.

23
00:02:15,103 --> 00:02:17,958
He collected a lot of tea in his glass jar, and he didn't want to waste it.

24
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:25,402
One time, he tried to mix different types of tea together and brew them.

25
00:02:25,402 --> 00:02:29,710
The milk tea made out of mixed tea is so much richer.

26
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:39,445
This is a mixture of six different types of tea.

27
00:02:39,445 --> 00:02:44,460
This is what we call a stocking bag.

28
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:48,995
We use water that's 100°C (212°F) hot.

29
00:02:48,995 --> 00:02:55,454
And we boil the tea and water together.

30
00:02:55,454 --> 00:03:02,024
When you see bubbles, it's time to pull the tea.

31
00:03:02,024 --> 00:03:34,282
Let it boil again, and pull again.

32
00:03:34,282 --> 00:03:42,609
You have to repeat this process six times.

33
00:03:42,609 --> 00:03:52,422
The tea leaves have to be seeped long enough to bring out the color and fragrance.

34
00:03:52,422 --> 00:04:02,410
For every cup of tea, we add slightly over 20% of milk.

35
00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:05,674
That's it.

36
00:04:05,674 --> 00:04:11,619
When I arrive every morning, the first thing I do is make myself a cup of milk tea.

37
00:04:11,619 --> 00:04:21,130
I try it, I make sure the quality is good before serving it to the customers.

38
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:27,837
[English] Cha chaan teng became really popular in the 1960s as Hong Kong's working class population grew.

39
00:04:27,837 --> 00:04:36,947
The dishes, which were a mix of eastern and western food like instant noodles, macaroni, and canned meat, were cheap and convenient.

40
00:04:36,947 --> 00:04:44,838
At these spots, you usually eat with spoons and forks, not chopsticks.

41
00:04:44,838 --> 00:04:49,359
[粤语] Our menu only has around 10 dishes.

42
00:04:49,359 --> 00:04:52,230
Basically staples that cater to all types of customers.

43
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:56,989
The customers already know what they want as soon as they arrive.

44
00:04:56,989 --> 00:05:02,793
If I ever change the menu, the customers may not like it anymore.

45
00:05:02,793 --> 00:05:05,644
Old shops like us also have a human touch.

46
00:05:05,644 --> 00:05:09,205
Traditional cha chaan teng have some similar elements.

47
00:05:09,205 --> 00:05:15,107
We have a counter, folded chairs, flies, and foul language.

48
00:05:15,107 --> 00:05:19,822
The customers have been coming here since they were small.

49
00:05:19,822 --> 00:05:24,539
They don't mind if it's not pretty, glamorous, or cozy here.

50
00:05:24,539 --> 00:05:27,605
This is what they look for here.

51
00:05:27,605 --> 00:05:38,220
They are like our friends. ⏩

52
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:43,314
[English] But when the pandemic struck, some cha chaan tengs were forced to close.

53
00:05:43,314 --> 00:05:46,048
Profit margins weren't that good to start with.

54
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:51,464
For those that are still in business, their owners have had to get creative.

55
00:05:51,464 --> 00:05:58,975
[粤语] When we think about a signature dish we must preserve from our cha chaan teng, it would definitely be egg tarts.

56
00:05:58,975 --> 00:06:09,658
Our version has caramel lava in it.

57
00:06:09,658 --> 00:06:13,215
We created different flavors of lava egg tarts.

58
00:06:13,215 --> 00:06:31,432
For example, we have Yuenyeung (tea and coffee mix), Horlicks, Ovaltine, and a taro sago flavor.

59
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:37,321
Pineapple bun is another very traditional cha chaan teng dish.

60
00:06:37,321 --> 00:06:48,360
We also came up with a new flavor and made a Peking Duck roll.

61
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:57,485
Our beverage makers also experimented a lot with traditional cha chaan teng drinks that would go well with coffee.

62
00:06:57,485 --> 00:07:01,435
They found that Horlicks goes very well with coffee.

63
00:07:01,435 --> 00:07:06,962
It's a very local drink, so we launched this drink called Horlicks Latte.

64
00:07:06,962 --> 00:07:11,746
Tai On was a cha chaan teng that opened in 1969.

65
00:07:11,746 --> 00:07:33,771
They had been in Yau Ma Tei for decades.

66
00:07:33,771 --> 00:07:43,497
We heard that the owner Mr Chan was going to move to Australia and didn't have plans for the restaurant.

67
00:07:43,497 --> 00:07:46,897
So we asked if we could take over the business.

68
00:07:46,897 --> 00:08:10,615
We wanted to preserve it because not many cha chaan teng with over 50 years of history remain today.

69
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,693
Our way is to keep it exactly the same.

70
00:08:12,693 --> 00:08:17,632
You see the booth seats, the chairs, a bar at the corner, and the glass doors.

71
00:08:17,632 --> 00:08:30,743
But with the food, I had doubts we could sustain our business if we still sold traditional items like ham macaroni, or ham and egg sandwiches.

72
00:08:30,743 --> 00:08:43,161
We wanted to combine cha chaan teng flavors with cafe food, so that people are wowed by the new flavors.

73
00:08:43,161 --> 00:08:48,569
We like this kind of retro-looking restaurant with new features.

74
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:53,827
Many people like to come here.

75
00:08:53,827 --> 00:08:58,500
【顾客】The tastes and textures of the food here are better than the traditional ones.

76
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,094
Actually it seems weird to me.

77
00:09:00,094 --> 00:09:07,981
I want the original taste and look.

78
00:09:07,981 --> 00:09:12,466
I wouldn't say a change is not good.

79
00:09:12,466 --> 00:09:16,281
But still, I miss those oily floors.

80
00:09:16,281 --> 00:09:20,306
【店主】In fact many people criticized us.

81
00:09:20,306 --> 00:09:24,297
Some of them called us soulless.

82
00:09:24,297 --> 00:09:30,055
The market will decide our future.

83
00:09:30,055 --> 00:09:39,106
If our food is not good, or people dislike the changes we made, then we'll be forced out of business.

84
00:09:39,106 --> 00:09:44,193
For now, it's still too early to decide if we are doing a good job or not.

85
00:09:44,193 --> 00:09:47,926
I like the new cha chaan tengs.

86
00:09:47,926 --> 00:09:51,320
As the world evolves, we can't always stay in the past.

87
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:56,420
[English] Hi guys it's me again! I'm Angie, who produced episode 2 of City Bites Hong Kong.

88
00:09:56,420 --> 00:10:00,953
As a Hong Konger, Cha Chaan Teng is definitely something I can't live without.

89
00:10:00,953 --> 00:10:03,555
Honestly, the food is nothing fancy.

90
00:10:03,555 --> 00:10:08,324
Does it really taste that good? Not always.

91
00:10:08,324 --> 00:10:14,327
But whenever I don't want to think, it's just very easy and comforting to pop into one.

92
00:10:14,327 --> 00:10:22,976
In this episode, I also wanted to bring out the debate of whether it's better to hold onto the tradition or evolve it into something new.

93
00:10:22,976 --> 00:10:25,978
Please share your thoughts with me in the comment section!

94
00:10:25,978 --> 00:10:30,843
And yes, do stay tuned for our coming episodes.

95
00:10:30,843 --> 00:10:33,343
In the next episode, we explore the menu at a local Dai Pai Dong, a type of restaurant in Hong Kong that's known for their heavenly stir-fries.

